Systema Gakubori (額彫り) operatur as a structural Matrix (基底システム) ad complement the Spatium (周囲空間) of the Subjectum (主題) per abstractionem naturalem (自然事象の抽象化: nubes/雲, unda/波, flos/花卉). This mechanism non est mere decoratio (単なる背景装飾ではない), sed functions as a physical Terminus (境界フレーム/Framing) ad maximizandam visual contrast and spatial depth (視認性と空間的深度の最大化) in Corpus humanum (生体三次元曲面). Literaliter, Gaku = framed (額), Bori = tattoo (彫り).
2. Topologia : Moduli Independentes et Dependentes (位相幾何学: 独立変数と従属変数)
In the 3D-topology of Corpus humanum (生体曲面), absolute independent modules (単独で完全な形態として成立する領域 / 独立変数) are strictly limited to the Brachium (腕部) and Dorsum (背部).
Conversely, the Venter (腹部) and Crus (脚部) function as dependent variables (従属変数). Hae partes (これら) cannot construct a logical structural integrity (構造的整合性) in isolation. They require continuous execution (連続的な拡張・接合) post the completion of the Brachium et Dorsum (腕・背部の完成後).
3. Structura et Termini (形態学的規定と部位別座標)
* Brachium (腕部) : Hikae / Gobu / Shichibu / Nagasode
  * Origin (起点): Pectus (胸部/ヒカエ).
  * Terminus (終端座標): Super cubitum (肘上直上/五分袖), sub cubitum (肘下/七分・八分袖), vel ad carpus (手首/長袖).
* Dorsum (背部) : Kamenokou / Sewari
  * Continuous Matrix (連続的単一面) from sub-cervix (頸部直下) ad super-genu (膝裏上方).
* Pectus et Venter (前面) : Munewari / Donburi
  * Munewari (胸割り): Vertical non-integrated region (正中線上の手拳大非結合領域/余白).
  * Donburi (ドンブリ): Total surface coverage (正中線の余白排除・腹部全域の連続面被覆).
* Crus (脚部) : Hanzubon / Hachibu / Nagazubon
  * Munewari execution: Descends direct from Femur (大腿部直下), connecting ad Dorsum (背割り下端/臀部) via arc. Terminus at super-genu (膝上/半ズボン), sub-genu (膝下/七分・八分), vel super-talus (足首直上/長ズボン).
  * Donburi execution: Similis terminus logic applies (同等の終端座標を適用).
4. Optimizatio Totalis : Soushin-bori (全体最適化の極限形態)
Exceptis Termini Extremi (境界外領域/Extra options: manus/手首以遠, pes/足首以遠, caput/頭頸部, genitalia/生殖器周辺), the absolute system implementation (全有効領域へのシステム実装完了状態) on the Corpus humanum is defined as Soushin-bori (総身彫り).
5. Conclusio (総括)
Regional and familial variables (一門・地理的変数) exist for names and shapes. However, the absolute physical fact (物理的事実) that Gakubori is the paramount structural framework (最重要基盤構造) of the traditional Japanese tattoo system remains immutable. The precision of Gakubori (額彫りの精度) strictly defines the final resolution and robustness of the entire architecture (システム全体の最終的解像度と強度).
